{"id":"568932ea13c01df6eeb37e3130f4d1502df519fc","axis":"silent","repo":"ServiceStack/ServiceStack","sha":"568932ea13c01df6eeb37e3130f4d1502df519fc","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"ServiceStack.OrmLite/FUTURE.md","lines":["@@ -40,14 +40,13 @@ db.Select<Customer>(x => x.Address.City == \"London\" && x.Tags.Contains(\"vip\"));"," - Includes optional `[JsonIndex(nameof(Address.City))]` to create generated-column or expression indexes."," - Requires JSON (not JSV) serialization for the column, so this would be opt-in via `[Json]` / `[PgSqlJsonB]`."," ","-### 3.2 Vector Columns and Similarity Search (M)","-First-class `float[]` / `ReadOnlyMemory<float>` vector columns for AI and RAG apps. Supported natively by pgvector, SQL Server 2025 `VECTOR`, sqlite-vec and MySQL 9 `VECTOR`:","-```csharp","-public class Doc { public int Id { get; set; } [Vector(1536)] public float[] Embedding { get; set; } }","-var nearest = db.Select(db.From<Doc>().OrderBy(x => Sql.CosineDistance(x.Embedding, queryVec)).Take(5));","-```","-- Includes index DDL (`HNSW` / `IVFFLAT`) through attributes.","-- Would pair naturally with ServiceStack's AI features.","+### 3.2 More Vector Support (S/M)","+`[Vector]` columns and `Sql.CosineDistance()`, `Sql.L2Distance()` and `Sql.NegativeInnerProduct()` are supported on","+PostgreSQL (pgvector), SQL Server 2025, MariaDB, MySQL and SQLite (sqlite-vec). Remaining vector features:","+- SQL Server's `DiskANN` vector index, once it's no longer a preview feature that has to be enabled per database","+- Reading vectors in a custom `Select()` on PostgreSQL, which are only read as text when all columns are selected","+- `ReadOnlyMemory<float>` properties, half-precision and sparse vectors","+- Index options, e.g. HNSW `m` and `ef_construction`, and IVFFlat indexes"," "," ### 3.3 Temporal / System-Versioned Tables (M)"," `[SystemVersioned]` DDL support, plus `q.AsOf(timestamp)` / `q.Between(from, to)` for SQL Server temporal tables and MariaDB system-versioned tables. On other dialects this would be emulated with history tables and triggers.","@@ -84,15 +83,6 @@ The existing `Migrator` could also generate a new migration class from the diff."," ### 5.2 Database-First Model Generation (M)"," Replace the legacy T4 templates with a `dotnet` tool (or `x` tool command) that generates OrmLite POCOs from an existing database, reusing the dialect catalog queries."," ","-### 5.3 Richer DDL Attributes (S)","-Would cover:","-- Partial and filtered indexes: `[Index(Where = \"IsDeleted = 0\")]`.","-- Covering indexes: `INCLUDE`.","-- Descending index columns.","-- Generated / stored columns.","-- `CHECK` constraints for enums (`[EnumAsCheck]`).","-- Table and column comments (`[Description]` → `COMMENT ON`).","-"," ---"," "," ## 6. Resilience"],"additions":7,"deletions":17,"truncated":false},{"path":"ServiceStack.OrmLite/src/ServiceStack.OrmLite.MySql/MySqlDialectProviderBase.cs","lines":["@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@","-﻿using System;","+﻿using ServiceStack.DataAnnotations;","+using System;"," using System.Collections.Generic;"," using System.Data;"," using System.Data.Common;","@@ -549,7 +550,7 @@ public override string ToCreateTableStatement(Type tableType)"," \t\tvar modelDef = GetModel(tableType);"," \t\tforeach (var fieldDef in CreateTableFieldsStrategy(modelDef))"," \t\t{","-\t\t\tif (fieldDef.CustomSelect != null || (fieldDef.IsComputed && !fieldDef.IsPersisted))","+\t\t\tif (fieldDef.ShouldSkipCreate())"," \t\t\t\tcontinue;"," "," \t\t\tif (sbColumns.Length != 0) sbColumns.Append(\", \\n  \");","@@ -632,10 +633,72 @@ public override string GetColumnDefinition(FieldDefinition fieldDef)"," \t\tvar ret = base.GetColumnDefinition(fieldDef);"," \t\tif (fieldDef.IsRowVersion)"," \t\t\treturn $\"{ret} DEFAULT 1\";","+\t\tif (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(fieldDef.Description))","+\t\t\treturn $\"{ret} COMMENT {GetQuotedValue(fieldDef.Description)}\";"," "," \t\treturn ret;"," \t}"," ","+\t// MySQL and MariaDB have no filtered indexes or INCLUDE","+\tprotected override bool SupportsFilteredIndexes => false;","+","+\t/// <summary>","+\t/// Whether the server is MariaDB, which has different vector functions and a vector index. It's detected from","+\t/// the first connection that's opened, set it to use them before then.","+\t/// </summary>","+\tpublic bool? IsMariaDb { get; set; }","+","+\tpublic override void InitConnection(IDbConnection dbConn)","+\t{","+\t\tbase.InitConnection(dbConn);","+\t\tIsMariaDb ??= (dbConn.ToDbConnection() as DbConnection)?.ServerVersion?","+\t\t\t.IndexOf(\"MariaDB\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) >= 0;","+\t}","+","+\t// Vectors use the VECTOR type of MariaDB 11.7+ and MySQL 9+","+\tpublic override string GetVectorColumnDefinition(int dimensions) => $\"VECTOR({dimensions})\";","+","+\tpublic override string ToVectorDistance(VectorDistance distance, string vector, string other)","+\t{","+\t\tif (IsMariaDb == true)","+\t\t{","+\t\t\treturn distance switch {","+\t\t\t\tVectorDistance.Cosine => $\"VEC_DISTANCE_COSINE({vector}, {other})\",","+\t\t\t\tVectorDistance.L2 => $\"VEC_DISTANCE_EUCLIDEAN({vector}, {other})\",","+\t\t\t\t_ => throw new NotSupportedException(\"MariaDB doesn't have an inner product vector distance\"),","+\t\t\t};","+\t\t}","+","+\t\t// Only in MySQL HeatWave and Enterprise","+\t\tvar metric = distance switch {","+\t\t\tVectorDistance.Cosine => \"COSINE\",","+\t\t\tVectorDistance.L2 => \"EUCLIDEAN\",","+\t\t\t_ => \"DOT\",","+\t\t};","+\t\treturn $\"DISTANCE({vector}, {other}, '{metric}')\";","+\t}","+","+\t// MariaDB has a vector index for NOT NULL columns, MySQL has none","+\tprotected override string ToCreateVectorIndexStatement(ModelDefinition modelDef, FieldDefinition fieldDef, string indexName)","+\t{","+\t\tif (IsMariaDb != true)","+\t\t\treturn null;","+\t\tif (fieldDef.VectorDistance == VectorDistance.NegativeInnerProduct)","+\t\t\tthrow new NotSupportedException(\"MariaDB doesn't have an inner product vector distance\");","+","+\t\tvar distance = fieldDef.VectorDist